{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And as for me, when I came from Paddan.</b> Since he is now commanding Joseph to bury him in the cave of Machpelah, he therefore makes his excuse to him for not burying Rachel his mother there just as he buried Leah there. And for this reason he says, <b>Rachel died upon me in the land of Canaan</b>, to say that she died in the land of Canaan and was not buried outside the land, but rather she died suddenly on the road and he could not bring her there to the cave of Machpelah because of the burden of the children and the heaviness of the livestock — for how could he leave them on the road and go there? And even if he had taken them along with him, they would not have arrived there except after many days, even though the cave was not far from there but only about half a day's distance. And for this reason he said 'she died upon me on the road' — for on the road she died, but she was not buried on the road, rather in Ramah, which is a city in the territory of Benjamin. And this is what it says." "<b>And I buried her there on the road to Efrat.</b> It would have been enough for Scripture to say 'and I buried her there,' since it had already said <b>on the road, when there was still some distance to come to Efrat.</b> But it comes to allude to what the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded, that by divine instruction he buried her there, so that she might be a help to her children when Nevuzaradan would exile them. And this is what Jeremiah the prophet said (Jeremiah 31:15): ״קול ברמה נשמע נהי בכי תמרורים רחל מבכה על בניה״. And for this reason Scripture elaborated: 'and I buried her there on the road to Efrat, which is Bethlehem' — that is, on the road by which her children would pass; and all this was by way of making an excuse to Joseph so that he would not be displeased. But Jacob's intention in not bringing her there was that he would be embarrassed before his forefathers if he were to bury two sisters together. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:08.852622278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}